== Notes ==
* Chub is often paired with Chargers in the boss room.
** {{dlc+|a}} She can also be paired with {{e|Drowned Charger}}s.{{dlc-}}
* When using {{i|Dr. Fetus}}' bomb combined with a shot type that passes through enemies, Chub will not eat the bomb.
* Each segment of Chub can be individually damaged, so a single piercing tear could hit Chub multiple times.
** {{Dlc|r}} Piercing shots no longer damage segmented enemies multiple times per attack.
* Chub will eat {{e|Troll Bomb}}s (such as those set by other bosses) just like bombs dropped by Isaac.
* {{i|Best Friend}} can damage Chub if eaten, similar to a bomb.
* {{i|Meat Cleaver}} can instantly kill Chub.
* Chub can spawn without the last segment.

== Trivia ==
* Chub appeared in the original ''Binding of Isaac.''
** Sometimes, in the original game, Chub would spawn with only two segments, preventing her from spawning anything. This can also happen in [[Repentance]].
* {{e|Carrion Queen}} is the posthumous version of her, and {{e|C.H.A.D.}} is the alternate version.
* She is the boss version of the Chargers.
* Chub is one of four bosses to have its posthumous version in the same chapter, the other cases being {{e|Gemini}} having {{e|Blighted Ovum}} in [[chapter 1]], {{dlc+|a}} {{e|Polycephalus}} having {{e|The Stain}} in [[chapter 2]]{{dlc-}} {{dlc+|r}} and the {{e|Tuff Twins}} having {{e|The Shell}} in [[Chapters|Chapter 2.5]]{{dlc-}}.
** However, Chub doesn't appear in the same environment as Carrion Queen, who appears in the {{s|Catacombs}} while Chub appears in The Caves and the {{dlc|a}} Flooded Caves.
* {{dlc|na+}} Prior to [[Booster Packs#Booster Pack #5|Booster Pack #5]], Chub could spawn {{e|Drowned Charger}}s if she was fought in the {{s|Flooded Caves}}. 
* Chub is female.<ref>http://web.archive.org/web/20120627122240/http://www.formspring.me/EdmundM/q/341049925531883948</ref>
* Chub may also be a reference to the Dodongos from ''[[wikipedia:The Legend of Zelda|The Legend of Zelda]]'', which Link had to toss bombs into their mouths to kill. This is supported by the Rules Card's display of "CHUB DISLIKES SMOKE", a reference to "DODONGO DISLIKES SMOKE" from the original ''Legend of Zelda''.
* {{dlc+|a+}} {{e|The Matriarch}} is a boss from [[Booster Pack #5]] that is simultaneously based on Chub, {{e|Fistula}}, and {{e|Fistuloid}}. When at low HP, she will split into a medium-sized Fistula, two small Fistulas, a Fistuloid and Chub.{{dlc-}}
** Unlike the usual pattern, if the Chub from The Matriarch eats a bomb, she'll spit it back at the player.
* Chub is one of the four bosses that can be spawned by {{e|It Lives!}}, the other three being {{e|Fistula|r}}, {{e|Polycephalus}}, and {{e|Teratoma}}.

